{"duration_api_ms":32991,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3a7d2fbf-3375-41ba-9478-f494bf53b669","total_cost_usd":2.5384368,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308571,"cache_read_input_tokens":7564,"output_tokens":3417,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1400},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308571,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":7564,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":272334},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3417,"cacheReadInputTokens":7564,"cacheCreationInputTokens":308571,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.5384368,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1400,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json` and coded **rung 2, \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents\"**, for Benjamin Allen on `egi-draft-a1v2`.\n\n**Evidence: AB 1955 (2023-2024), one record across two passages**\n- **Vote page:** Allen voted Aye on final Senate passage of the Senate-amended text on 2024-06-13. The vote was 29-8. That is about 22% No, so the near-unanimous rule doesn't apply. The vote falls in his current term, which began 2022-12-05.\n  - `actor_quote`: \"Ayes (29): Allen, Archuleta\"\n  - `tally_quote`: \"Result: PASS, 29-8.\"\n- **Bill text:** the provision quote comes from §220.5(a), the operative section. It says schools \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent.\n\n**Why rung 2 and not a neighbouring rung**\n- **The preemption rule doesn't make it adjacent.** That rule (H12) only applies when no rung is about which level of government decides. Here the question itself is \"who decides,\" and rung 2 is about forbidding these rules. So the bill is on-question.\n- **It doesn't reach rung 1.** §220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required to disclose.\" It doesn't require staff to keep the information from parents.\n- **It rules out rungs 3–5,** because it voids local rules that would require schools to tell parents.\n- **I treated the bill as single-subject.** Its other parts (resources for parents and a ban on retaliating against staff) are about the same pupil-rights subject.\n\n**Judgement calls a reviewer may read differently**\n- Whether a bill that voids local disclosure mandates fully matches rung 2, given its carve-out \"unless otherwise required by state or federal law.\"\n- Whether the single-subject reading of the bill holds.\n\n`quotes` is empty because there are no sources with Allen's own words, and `needs_source` is empty because nothing the row needed was missing. The chair rests on one instrument, so code will compute the evidence tier as `single-source`.","ttft_ms":14467,"type":"result","duration_ms":36173,"uuid":"2be9d621-8ce4-49f7-b379-c22fdb11f712","ttft_stream_ms":1382,"time_to_request_ms":97,"first_content_frame_ms":1383,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
